      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure if this is the right/best way to construct the target `SkColorSpace`.  But IIUC this is what [the legacy code does](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/pdfium/core/fxcodec/png/libpng_png_decoder.cpp;l\u003d81-96;drc\u003d553e531de10b8096779b3d3c77724781f6cfe0e4).  But maybe we should get the screen color profile in a more-accurate, not-just-gamma-encompassing way?\n\nFWIW we had to do quite a few tweaks (hacks?) in https://crbug.com/388025081 to match legacy Blink decoder\u0027s handling of gamma values.  And in the end the Skia code is more accurate than `libpng` (e.g. Skia doesn\u0027t assume that 2.2 is a neutral gamma).\n\nIs this worth following up on?  Maybe I should open a separate bug?  Maybe loop in @ccameron for color-space questions?",
